course: dictionary
lesson: 8453
title: Said and other speech words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: When someone speaks in a story, the writer often uses a speech verb to show who spoke. The most common one is «said», the past form of say. «"Hello," said the fox.» The fox spoke, and said tells you that it happened in the past.
explain: Readers hardly notice said, so it is often the best choice. Other speech verbs add detail when you use them now and then. Whispered means spoken very quietly, and shouted means spoken very loudly. «"Stop!" shouted Liam.» The word shouted tells you how loud he was.
explain: In old or formal writing, said can mean the one already named. In «the said house», said means the house that was already mentioned. Look at the words around it to find out which house the writer means.
explain: Commas go around the said part when speech is split. «"I'm ready," said Mia, smiling.» The comma after ready comes before the closing speech marks, and the words after said start with a small letter because the sentence carries on.
fact: Said is the past form of say. Say, says, said and saying are all forms of the same verb.
fact: «Mom said yes.» means Mom spoke in the past and answered yes.
fact: «The said house» is an old or formal use, and it means the house already named.
fact: Other speech verbs include asked, shouted, whispered and muttered. Use them now and then to add detail.
fact: In split speech, put commas around the said part: «"Come here," said Dad.»
exercise: «"Hello," said the fox.» Which word tells you the fox spoke? | fox | *said | hello | forest
exercise: «Mom said yes.» What form of say is said here? | The future form of say | The plural of say | A noun for a loud sound | *The past form of say
exercise: In «the said house», what does said mean? | A very old house | A house that has been sold | A loud house | *The house already named
test: Fill the gap with a speech verb that shows a quiet voice: «"Shh," ___ Nadia.» | shouted | cooked | asked | *whispered
test: Which sentence has the commas in the right place? | "Come here". said Dad. | *"Come here," said Dad. | "Come here." said Dad. | "Come here," said, Dad.
exam: In «Liam said, "The bus is late."», which word is the speech verb? | *said | Liam | bus | late
